  "date": "11 October 2026",
  "summary_en": "The Phasor Noise node procedurally generates wave-like noise by summing local phasor kernels, each defining sine and cosine waves in a small area. It suits wood grain, water ripples and wind-blown textures, with finer control over direction and spacing than OpenCL sine and cosine code.",
  "inputs": [
    "size_ref: sets output image size and metadata",
    "pos (optional): UV layer replacing pixel coordinates",
    "time (optional): per-pixel time value",
    "bias (optional): sets wave peak positions for Phasor Wave",
    "scale (optional): multiplies Element Size",
    "direction (optional): UV layer setting the initial kernel angle"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Signature / Rotate Channel: layer type; non-Mono signatures give one noise per channel, each rotated by an offset",
    "Amplitude / Center / Noise Contrast: scale, offset and contrast of noise values",
    "Type: Phasor Wave (Sine, Rectangle or Saw profile), Phasor Noise, Gabor Noise or Intensity Field",
    "Element Size / Element Scale: wave width, with per-axis scaling",
    "Offset / Tile Size: shift and repeat period",
    "Wave Bias / Blending Radius / Kernels / Seed: peak position, kernel overlap, kernel count, randomness",
    "3D Noise (Animate, Pulse Length, Time Scale, Loop Length): third dimension for animation and seamless loops",
    "Rotate Pattern / Rotation Varying: kernel angles, uniform or randomised, with optional secondary set",
    "Post Processing (Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum): applied in the listed order"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Procedural patterns can look more artificial than simulation-based results.",
    "Values can fall outside 0 to 1 after amplitude or contrast changes; use a Clamp COP to enforce a range.",
    "Element Size values outside 0 to 1 can give unwanted results.",
    "With Tile Size enabled, some parameters are rounded or clamped to stay tileable."
  ],
  "resume_fr": "Le nœud Phasor Noise génère un bruit ondulatoire procédural en sommant des noyaux phaseurs locaux, adapté aux veines de bois, aux ondulations d'eau et aux textures de vent."
